  "_comment": "PROVISIONAL. UNIFIED whole-master registration of the TWW3 Old World mod parchment (tww3_old_world_mod_parchment.png, 4096x4096), superseding the five separate per-region crop registrations (tww3_old_world_mod_parchment_{bretonnia,empire,kislev_norsca,dark_lands,badlands_nehekhara}) for whole-map work. Rather than a new crop, the user re-marked the SAME paired anchor dots the five per-region crops already carry directly on the uncropped master image, plus bridge dots not found in any per-region seed. DETECTION: a compact (4-16px, roughly square/plus-shaped) group of pixels in a colour that does not appear ANYWHERE in either original, undotted document (sources/originals/tww3_old_world_mod_parchment.png and sources/originals/terraqueous_globe_reprojected.png). Kept components need chroma (max-min channel) >=120 everywhere, OR >=40 outside the one known noisy rectangle (master px x:[3600,4100] y:[2250,3100], the Old Dwarf Road/Scalded Delta linework crossing where re-save/anti-alias noise concentrates) -- the pale-dot fix from the Parravon pass. Colour-paired between the two dots sheets (exact match, greedy nearest-predicted-position for a colour used 2+ times, a whole-set least-squares affine through the unambiguous single matches as the predictor). 2026-09-10: the dots_source sheets moved from sources/dots/ to sources/dots_4/ (the user's own reorganization into numbered dots_N/ batch folders -- unrelated to the '- dots_N' filename suffix, which is a per-region iteration counter, not a folder name); tools/worldgen/sources.py's SOURCE_SUBDIRS search list was extended to include dots_3/ and dots_4/ so dots_source (still a bare filename here) keeps resolving. The same move also carried an intentional revert: the 5 Dark Lands dots added in the immediately-prior pass (which had pushed this seed to 85 landmarks) are gone again, confirmed deliberate by the user rather than an accidental stale copy, and 'dark_lands_purple' (dropped in that same prior pass) is back. 81 landmarks total (66 matched to the five per-region seeds' own landmarks by exact canvas position, 15 new/bridge dots named 'c_<hex>', a repeated hex suffixed _2). objective=landmarks means NO silhouette fit (the drift-prone stage, and the whole-map silhouette fit is already known broken by the source's inconsistent inter-region scale -- see the landmark-accuracy-wall note), just thin-plate interpolation through the 81 dots. master_shape is the master's own (h,w)=(4096,4096); the source will be the dot-free master. This record only PLACES the whole parchment; no geometry is extracted yet.",
  "_comment_lattice": "16x16 over the full 4096x4096 master (~256 master px horizontal/vertical spacing). 81 landmarks blanket every one of the five regions plus the inter-region seams, so a lattice this dense (vs. 6x6 for badlands_nehekhara alone) is warranted and, per the landmarks-objective rule (fit_registration.py), bounded to the landmark hull + pad rather than the full frame (4+ landmarks makes the thin-plate kernel term nonzero, which blows up past the dots' hull).",
  "lattice": {
    "nx": 16,
    "ny": 16,
    "inset": 0.02
  },
